  "properties": {
    "title": "Free and Open Source AI Assisted Mapping : fAIr",
    "description": "fAIr is an open AI-assisted mapping platform developed by the Humanitarian OpenStreetMap Team (HOT). In this talk we will go through current progress and state of the art of usage of AI in humanitarian mapping. We will share our experience and roadmap of fAIr .\n\nThe service uses AI models, specifically computer vision techniques, to detect objects in satellite and UAV imagery.",
